2026-09-27T03:27:42.2979843Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2980138Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2980366Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2980940Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2981838Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2981977Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2982185Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2982442Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2982669Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2982747Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2982946Z ================
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2983076Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2983250Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2983545Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2983694Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2983817Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2984073Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2984226Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2984343Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2984667Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2984956Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2985419Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2985831Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2985945Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2986325Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2986744Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2986961Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2987168Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2987452Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2987513Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2987729Z ========
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2987853Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2988666Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2989472Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2989715Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2990072Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2990413Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2990856Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2991309Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2991978Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2992157Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2992562Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2992784Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2992954Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2993616Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2994469Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2994934Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2995990Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:27:42.2996149Z 
